  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "After a recent UI 2.0 update went live the overall performance of VRChat is now noticeably worse, especially in PC VR when the new menu is open. Also there is now a tiny lag/freeze every time when the quick menu is opened. Messing around in Performance settings didn't help that much compared to how VRChat would run before the update. Clearing different caches didn't help either. Using Oculus Quest 2 connected to PC via Link cable. My PC specs are i7-4790, 16GB DDR3 1600mhz, 1070ti, everything is running off an M.2 Nvme ssd. Not denying that my rig may be a bit dated, but it's sad to see VRChat being harder to run on older hardware.",
